:null,"result":"I'm blocking PKT-0132, not rejecting it. The code looks correct, but the packet's goal is a speed gain, and that gain still hasn't been shown. Another attempt can't change that until the factory gives a quiet machine to measure on.\n\n**What's done properly**\n- The previous review's lock problem is fixed. The Comments panel's add button now gets the same locks and enabled/disabled state as the toolbar's comment button, and it is added to `paragraphControls` and `lockControls`. The executor also found and fixed a second bug: the button stayed disabled after load. They added a check for both, `perf/comments-addnew-locks.cjs`.\n- The deferred build only runs in the document editor (`window.DE && appPrefix === 'de-'`). The `isViewBuilt` guard keeps the earlier wiring path for other editors.\n- When the add button is wired late, `Toolbar.js` stops listening for the build notification once it fires, so the wiring happens once.\n- The comparison against the original code passed on all 4 documents, with no change in behavior.\n- The Executor log is filled in. No follow-up packets were requested, so none are missing. The size is well under budget: 8 files and about 400 lines.\n\n**Why it can't be approved**\n- The goal is to make documents open faster, measured on an idle VM. Pooled over 32 pairs of runs, Ready came out 84 ms faster at the median. The run-to-run spread was −252 to +286 ms, and only 20 of 32 runs were faster. LoadDoc changed by +2 ms. That isn't a gain under the rule, and the executor says so themselves.\n- The comparison oracle's own timings are just as noisy. For example, \"join\" on `simple.rtf` went from 3537 to 5575 ms, and \"save\" on `styles.docx` from 406 to 2273 ms, with no related code change.\n- The VM's load average stayed between 3.4 and 6.0 because other factory agents were running. The previous reviewer asked for an idle VM. The executor couldn't get one, and no agent can arrange one.\n\n**What's needed**\nThe factory operator needs to give the packet an idle measurement slot, with no other agents on the VM. Then the 16-pair alternating-order runs on two documents with `open-window-build.js` can be repeated. If Ready improves by more than the spread, the packet can be approved. If it doesn't, the deferral doesn't meet the goal.\n\nVERDICT: BLOCK the factory operator must give an idle VM slot so the open-window A/B runs can be repeated, because the code is correct but the measured gain (−84 ms, spread −252 to +286 ms) is within the noise from concurrent agents","ttft_ms":3679,"type":"result","duration_ms":26273,"uuid":"5a720d7e-73c5-4e6a-8e1e-acf19646a8c3","ttft_stream_ms":2132,"time_to_request_ms":347,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":5,"system_prompt":246,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":5,"input_attachments":19,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":0,"transcript_persist":8,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":7,"init_frame_send":2,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":5,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":18,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":2,"request_build":7},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":27,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":127,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":212,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":140,"process_rss_mib_result":217,"process_anon_mib_result":131,"process_peak_rss_mib":246,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1012,"process_wall_ms_turn":26272,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":240,"process_wall_ms_streaming":15403,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_count":269,"main_stream_chunk_count":86,"process_turn_states":{"main_stream":{"cpu_ms":240,"wall_ms":15403,"entries":5},"tool":{"cpu_ms":64,"wall_ms":143,"entries":3},"first_event_wait":{"cpu_ms":468,"wall_ms":10256,"entries":5},"before_first_request":{"cpu_ms":127,"wall_ms":348,"entries":1},"between_requests":{"cpu_ms":101,"wall_ms":111,"e